 "trace": {
  "calibration": "see calibration.notes",
  "heights": "dia col 670: window frames rows 92-183 (3.03-1.91 m); navy to row 258, yellow line 258-261 (0.99-0.95 m), underframe from 262 (0.94 m); door col 470: leaves rows 65-261 (3.36-0.95), blue top band 62-65, yellow outline top 58-61 (3.45-3.41)",
  "cab.doors[0]": "Joint camera fit (p028, near side-on): cab door outline 1.24-2.05 m (diagram 1.08-1.84); p028 measured locally from heights (door 0.99-3.41 m = 319 px, yaw about 15 degrees): 0.80 m wide, 1.46 m from its rear to the next window's glass; window about half the door's width, in two panes (reader 2); its window toward the rear edge (both readers, p016/p028)",
  "cab.doors[1..2]": "Joint fit with the two doors' widths tied: door 1 leaves 5.48-7.12 m, door 2 14.89-16.53 m (1.64 m wide; the diagram draws 4.49-6.30 and 13.96-15.76). Leaf windows glass rows 83-176 (2.00-3.14 m)",
  "cab.windows": "Joint camera fit (match/joint.json: p028, p031, p113; p031's focal fixed from EXIF, 2439 px; 46 picks, fit rms 1.7-3.3 px, door widths tied): the window ahead of door 1 at 3.53-4.76 m; the saloon windows from 7.72 m to 14.12 m in the diagram's pattern (rescaled; back-projection on p031 puts window fronts at 9.03 and 10.92 m); the two behind door 2 back-projected on p031 at 16.71-17.73 and 18.25-19.52 m. The diagram (glass runs 327-414, 619-721, 755-875, 909-1028, 1062-1164, 1375-1477, 1511-1613 px) draws the cab car's layout about 0.5-1.0 m too far forward; its car 2 is kept. Heights: the photos' windows are the diagram's glass, not its outlines: 1.93-2.96 m",
  "next": "dia row 135 from 1765 px at 80.3 px/m: frames 1855-1967, 1991-2103, 2304-2416, 2440-2570, 2594-2723, 2747-2859, 3060-3172, 3196-3308; doors 2132-2275, 2888-3031",
  "bogies": "dia row 325: wheel chords centred 196/386 and 1374/1564 px (cab), 1909/2099 and 3064/3254 (car 2): bogie centres 2.60 and 17.35 m; the drawn wheelbase is 2.38 m against the published 2.6 m: the published figure is used",
  "nose.profile": "as before, but the face stays flat to 3.30 m and rolls back through 3.43 m: the old points (0, 3.40) then (0.1, 3.52) made the spline loop forward to 3.60 m and dip back to 3.52 m, a lip across the face's top that broke the paint there",
  "face": "First estimate on p082 (near head-on) at about 200 px/m both ways from the roof (sy 178 = 3.78 m) and the screens' centre line (sx 1065); refined by camera (see face.camera)",
  "face.lamps": "Joint fit (p028, p031, p113): head 0.79 m from the centre line, 1.59 m up; marker 1.22 m, 1.59 m; tail 1.04 m, 1.42 m (from 0.77/1.10/0.97 first read on p082); three per side, flush on the yellow, each in a thin black ring (readers 1 and 2); confirmed on a 444 (444016, held-out tail 1.8 cm); sizes from the second reader's pair check (render vs 450031/450113): headlamp 1.55x the marker and the tail, so head r 0.13, marker 0.055, tail 0.06 (positions unchanged: they come from the camera fit)",
  "face.screens": "p031 surface picks (match.py surface, solved camera): the glass's edges stand upright on the real train, inner 0.674-0.675 m and outer 1.286-1.288 m from the centre line, 2.15-2.20 to 3.13-3.16 m up; the frame's outer edge 1.30-1.32 m. The face is drawn in metres of a 1.4 m half-width scaled to the body's width at each height (1.39 m at the glass's foot, 1.33 m at its top: tumblehome), so the same upright edges are glass 0.678 to 0.713 m (inner, foot to top) and 1.293 to 1.359 m (outer), frame outer 1.319 to 1.383 m. The first reading took the real metres as drawn metres, which made the glass 4-10 cm too narrow, worst at the top (review of v3: 'the cab window is larger')",
  "face.number": "450082 head-on (f-face-082, 186 px/m up, 217 px/m across, from the glass): a thin white sans 0.45 m long, caps about 0.10 m tall, centred 0.03 m outboard of the glass's centre (0.985 m out), 0.19 m above the glass top (3.34 m); 450031 (a crop) agrees. Rendered light: Arial thinned, whose caps are 0.72 of `height` and whose six digits run 3.3x it, so height 0.155 (0.14 rendered 12% short of 450031 on the p031 camera); placed from the p031 surface pick (centre 1.034 m out on the real train at 3.34 m, where the body is 1.309 m wide: 1.106 m drawn)",
  "face.lower": "444016 (p016, close three-quarter; 231 px/m across from the lamps' spacing, 308 px/m up from the headlamp) and 450082 head-on (f-face-082; 164 px/m from the face's half-width): under the yellow the face carries on in body colour (navy; green on the 350) for 0.24-0.26 m, to 1.07 m (the valance), a grey anti-climber pad at each corner filling its height (0.90-1.30 m out, 1.08-1.31 m up); below that a ribbed black skirt box each side, eight slats, 0.76-1.30 m out (444016 0.68-1.26, 450082 0.74-1.17 near and 0.88-1.42 far), 1.07 down to 0.45 m (0.49 on 444016, 0.37 on 450082), and between the skirts the open recess the coupler stands in, black up to the gangway frame's foot (1.19 m). The same hardware on 350109 (head-on, Watford Junction). Before: dark from the lamp panel's foot down, one block; the recess is cut 0.16 m back into the chin (which stands 0.18 m proud of the face from 0.5 to 1.0 m), so the skirts either side stand out as boxes and the coupler sits back between them (444016, 450082: the coupler's face is about level with the yellow); its foot at 0.52 m, where the chin's underside turns back",
  "face.gangwayFrame": "Joint fit: the frame's front 0.55 m ahead of the face, half-width 0.60 m, 1.20-3.61 m; p028 shows it on bellows (g28b); bellows black ribbed rubber (p028 g28b, 444016); second reader (face pair on 450031): the frame's border about 0.17 of the door's width per side and it stands 20% less proud: half 0.52 m (0.355 m door), depth 0.45 m; colour a dark neutral grey",
  "roof, under": "not measured: the roof pods and underframe boxes as the old data had them (cab 8.5 m)",
  "livery": "Sampled on 350116 (p116, overcast, far side: medians of clean patches) and 350120 (p120, bodyside in shade, face in light), each normalised by one gain that brings its yellow gangway door to the p126 yellow (#ECB746; p116 x1.23, p120 x1.53): bodyside grey #858B91 upper and #66676B lower on p116, #767677-#7A7C76 on p120 (shade), so #7A7E83 (was #A0A5AC, the raw upper side in daylight: far too light, the review); the W stripes' green #21412F-#2D4D40 in shade on p116, livelier in light: #2F6B4E (was the diagram's #00A862); the pale stripes #7A9F9B: #8FAEA9; doors and dark stripes #282D2B, the cab end and face a dark teal-grey (p120 face #34584E raw, #4F8777 normalised in shade): one dark green-teal for both, #34504B (was #365E60). Yellow #ECB746 (p126 door). Before: {\"body\": \"#A0A5AC\", \"darkGreen\": \"#365E60\", \"green\": \"#00A862\", \"pale\": \"#B9CCCA\"}",
  "livery.map": "83:0, 169.3:1.24, 230:2.06, 327:3.53, 415:4.76, 442:5.48, 586:7.12, 619:7.72, 1165:14.12, 1198:14.89, 1342:16.53, 1375:16.70, 1478:17.85, 1511:18.25, 1614:19.50, 1708:20.34 (diagram px : metres), from the 450's joint fit",
  "livery.shapes": "trace.py on the diagram, rows 50-262, colours #024E47 (dark green: cab end, doors, stripes, car ends), #00BF6F (green: the W stripes and the car-end block), #BFD3D1 (pale green), #0B0B0B (the black window bands: only regions 1.0-1.3 m tall)",
  "face.gangway": "350120, 350109: the gangway door all yellow (four panels, no black part), in a weathered grey metal frame",
  "face.livery": "350120: the face dark grey above the lamps round the screens, the LNR teal-green where the SWR units are yellow (the outer strip and the lamp panel), a thin orange line across the top at the cantrail",
  "face.topLine": "p126, p120: a thin orange line across the face at the cantrail, continuing the bodyside's",
  "face.strip": "450082 head-on (f-face-082) and 450031/450113: the yellow on the face runs from the screen surround's outer edge (1.32 m, adjacent to the black frame) round the cab corner and up; head-on its band narrows from the corner side over the top 0.1-0.15 m and ends at about 3.40-3.45 m, so the inner edge curves out from the glass top (3.15 m; 450031: it has begun to lean out by the frame's top) to meet the outer edge at 3.40 m, where the crescent takes over: its front edge rounds back onto the side from there to the tip at 3.52 m (one edge, so no step where the two meet). On the side it continues as the crescent (livery.crescent), its top rounded at 3.49 m; the face strip draws the corner, the crescent only the part facing sideways, so the two views never disagree where the renderer blends them",
  "face.surround": "head-on 450082: the black frame stands 0.09 m above the glass (17 px at 186 px/m: 3.24 m, clear of the number) and 0.07 m outboard (1.32 m); earlier read through p031/p082 surfaces as 3.26-3.29 m, which put the number on the frame",
  "livery.branding": "LM-W (the LNR 'W' emblem, traced off 350126 at Crewe, logos/SOURCES.md), white on the teal cab end between the front corner and the cab door, on both sides (350126, 350116, 350105): on 350116 (p116) against the first window's 1.03 m height (200 px in the zoom) it stands 0.36 m tall, centred 2.19 m up (0.26 m above the window's foot); along the car on 350126 its centre is 0.10 m ahead of the cab door's front edge (1.24 m) by its own width (0.16 m = 62 px): 1.12 m, drawn at 0.98 m to clear the model's cab door grab rail (which stands ahead of the door's edge; on 350126 the emblem sits just ahead of that rail). The small 'West Midlands Trains' operator line by the cab door (350373) is not drawn"
 },
